-- Chapter 9, Section 9.5.7 — SQL placeholder arity (#309).
-- Features: db_effect, sql_provenance, check_error.
--
-- The SQL is literal (so no E207), but it has two ? placeholders while only one
-- parameter is supplied.  When both the SQL and the params array are statically
-- sized, that mismatch is a compile-time error (E208).
public fn mismatched(-> @Result<Array<Array<Option<String>>>, String>)
  requires(true)
  ensures(true)
  effects(<DB>)
{
  DB.query("SELECT * FROM u WHERE a = ? AND b = ?", [Some("x")])
}
